---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
import { WarningText } from "@i-dot-ai-npm/component-library-astro";
---

<ToolingLayout
  title="Get your AI Gateway key"
  currentPath="/tooling/get-your-key"
>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Get your AI Gateway key</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    All tools need an AI Gateway key, which connects to your budget allowance.
    You can:
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/keys/generate/personal">
        create a personal key
      </a>{" "}
      for personal use (such as, performance management or personal development)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/keys/generate/team">
        create a team key
      </a>{" "}
      for team work (such as, prototyping and evaluation) or community work
      (such as development to support your profession)
    </li>
    <li>
      contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel on i.AI Slack to create a
      product key (used by products directly)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <WarningText> Do not share your key with anybody else. </WarningText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Next steps</h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Once you have your key, follow the setup instructions to add it to your
    chosen tool:
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/opencode">
        Set up OpenCode
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/claude-code">
        Set up Claude Code
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/cursor">
        Set up Cursor
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/pi">
        Set up Pi
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</ToolingLayout>
